WEBVTT

00:00:00.543 --> 00:00:04.136
There are many islands in the sea near Scotland.

00:00:04.196 --> 00:00:08.127
This story is about one of these islands.

00:00:08.188 --> 00:00:11.790
The name of the island is Lana.

00:00:11.849 --> 00:00:16.392
Lana isn't big, but it's very beautiful.

00:00:16.452 --> 00:00:19.024
It's very quiet too.

00:00:19.084 --> 00:00:23.927
There are no houses, or roads, or cars on Lana.

00:00:23.987 --> 00:00:26.088
But there's a castle.

00:00:26.148 --> 00:00:29.796
The castle is very old.

00:00:29.856 --> 00:00:33.942
A young Scotsman lives in the castle.

00:00:34.002 --> 00:00:38.663
The Scotsman's name is Duncan McTaddish.

00:00:38.723 --> 00:00:44.004
Duncan lives in the castle with his dog, Jock.

00:00:44.064 --> 00:00:48.495
Duncan is very happy on his island.

00:00:48.555 --> 00:00:51.616
He likes going for walks with Jock.

00:00:51.676 --> 00:00:56.267
He likes swimming and fishing in his little boat.

00:00:56.327 --> 00:01:00.500
There are many big rooms in Duncan's castle.

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:08.534
They have a lot of old things in them, pictures and heavy tables, chairs and beds.

00:01:08.594 --> 00:01:13.426
In winter, the castle is very cold and dark.

00:01:13.486 --> 00:01:19.798
Duncan puts on a lot of electric lights in all the rooms.

00:01:19.858 --> 00:01:25.869
One Monday morning in April, Duncan gets a letter.

00:01:25.929 --> 00:01:27.660
What's this?

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:29.250
He asks.

00:01:29.310 --> 00:01:31.781
He opens the letter.

00:01:31.841 --> 00:01:35.172
It's from the electricity company.

00:01:35.232 --> 00:01:43.066
Duncan reads, electricity from October to March 5,000 pounds.

00:01:43.126 --> 00:01:49.458
Oh, Duncan says, I haven't got 5,000 pounds.

00:01:49.518 --> 00:01:51.119
What can I do?

00:01:51.139 --> 00:01:54.130
He's very unhappy.

00:01:54.190 --> 00:01:57.521
I can do only one thing.

00:01:57.581 --> 00:01:59.648
Sell my island.

00:01:59.708 --> 00:02:02.436
And my castle!

00:02:02.496 --> 00:02:06.518
Duncan telephones a man in London.

00:02:06.578 --> 00:02:10.501
The man's name is Mr. Moneybags.

00:02:10.561 --> 00:02:15.644
Mr. Moneybags sells houses and castles.

00:02:15.704 --> 00:02:22.588
I want to sell my island and my castle, Duncan says.

00:02:22.648 --> 00:02:27.044
Okay, Mr. Moneybag says.

00:02:27.104 --> 00:02:31.480
Two days later, he telephones Duncan.

00:02:31.540 --> 00:02:37.144
Leaping Larry wants to buy your island, he says.

00:02:37.204 --> 00:02:39.636
Leaping, who?

00:02:39.696 --> 00:02:41.276
Duncan asks.

00:02:41.336 --> 00:02:47.420
Leaping Larry, you know, the famous American rock star.

00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:51.694
He wants to buy your island for his girlfriend.

00:02:51.753 --> 00:02:56.346
A rock star, Duncan says.

00:02:56.406 --> 00:03:03.729
He wants to see the island tomorrow afternoon, Mr. Moneybag says.

00:03:03.788 --> 00:03:05.039
Is that okay?

00:03:05.059 --> 00:03:09.342
Er, yes, Duncan says.

00:03:09.402 --> 00:03:12.604
Yes, of course.

00:03:12.664 --> 00:03:19.228
Leaping Larry and his girlfriend are coming to the island by helicopter.

00:03:19.288 --> 00:03:21.450
They're very late.

00:03:21.510 --> 00:03:25.377
Duncan and Jock wait a long time.

00:03:25.437 --> 00:03:29.184
Then the helicopter arrives.

00:03:29.244 --> 00:03:34.108
A tall man with long dark hair gets down from it.

00:03:34.168 --> 00:03:37.550
He's about 45 years old.

00:03:37.610 --> 00:03:39.812
There's a girl with him.

00:03:39.872 --> 00:03:44.796
She's about 20 and has long yellow hair.

00:03:44.855 --> 00:03:47.758
There's a small animal with her.

00:03:47.818 --> 00:03:52.111
The animal has long white hair.

00:03:52.171 --> 00:03:55.128
Hi, the man says.

00:03:55.188 --> 00:04:01.178
I'm leaping Larry, and this is my girlfriend, Roxanne.

00:04:01.238 --> 00:04:04.211
Hi, Roxanne says.

00:04:04.270 --> 00:04:07.743
This is my dog, Bobo.

00:04:07.803 --> 00:04:10.786
Larry looks at the castle.

00:04:10.846 --> 00:04:15.248
Look at that old castle, Roxanne, he says.

00:04:15.308 --> 00:04:18.050
Don't you love it, honey?

00:04:18.110 --> 00:04:20.973
Roxanne doesn't smile.

00:04:21.032 --> 00:04:24.050
It's only an old castle.

00:04:24.110 --> 00:04:28.870
Leaping Larry and Roxanne go into the castle.

00:04:28.929 --> 00:04:30.920
It's very dark.

00:04:30.980 --> 00:04:33.593
Leaping Larry can't see.

00:04:33.652 --> 00:04:35.894
He falls down.

00:04:35.954 --> 00:04:38.126
Where are the lights?

00:04:38.186 --> 00:04:39.766
He asks.

00:04:39.826 --> 00:04:43.028
I'm sorry, Duncan says.

00:04:43.088 --> 00:04:45.470
There isn't any light.

00:04:45.530 --> 00:04:50.284
The company stopped my electricity this morning.

00:04:50.344 --> 00:04:54.966
I want some hard food, Roxanne says.

00:04:55.026 --> 00:04:57.998
I'm sorry, Duncan says.

00:04:58.058 --> 00:05:00.951
But I can't make hot food.

00:05:01.010 --> 00:05:03.962
I haven't got any electricity.

00:05:04.022 --> 00:05:06.744
But there is some cold food.

00:05:06.804 --> 00:05:10.146
Cold food, Roxanne says.

00:05:10.206 --> 00:05:12.168
Now thank you.

00:05:12.228 --> 00:05:14.189
I'm going to bed.

00:05:14.248 --> 00:05:17.610
But first I want a hot bath.

00:05:17.670 --> 00:05:20.972
And Bobo wants a bath too.

00:05:21.032 --> 00:05:24.644
I'm very sorry, Duncan says.

00:05:24.703 --> 00:05:27.363
But there's no hot water.

00:05:27.423 --> 00:05:31.774
No nights, no food, no hot water.

00:05:31.834 --> 00:05:36.206
Roxanne says, I don't like this place.

00:05:36.266 --> 00:05:42.408
Now, honey, leaping Larry says, don't call me honey.

00:05:42.468 --> 00:05:47.060
Roxanne says, let's go Bobo.

00:05:47.120 --> 00:05:50.992
Roxanne and Bobo go to bed.

00:05:51.052 --> 00:05:55.384
Larry and Duncan eat cold food and talk.

00:05:55.444 --> 00:05:57.547
Jock watches.

00:05:57.607 --> 00:06:01.018
Suddenly, Roxanne screams.

00:06:01.078 --> 00:06:05.141
Duncan, Larry and Jock run to her room.

00:06:05.200 --> 00:06:08.583
Roxanne is in bed with Bobo.

00:06:08.642 --> 00:06:11.254
Honey, what's wrong?

00:06:11.314 --> 00:06:12.844
Larry asks.

00:06:12.904 --> 00:06:17.577
There was a noise in the room, Roxanne says.

00:06:17.637 --> 00:06:19.538
What was it?

00:06:19.597 --> 00:06:22.306
Duncan starts to smile.

00:06:22.366 --> 00:06:25.033
Why are you smiling?"

00:06:25.093 --> 00:06:26.564
Roxanne says.

00:06:26.624 --> 00:06:28.766
She's very angry.

00:06:28.826 --> 00:06:32.568
Look at Jock, Duncan says.

00:06:32.628 --> 00:06:35.480
Jock is under the bed.

00:06:35.540 --> 00:06:38.531
He has a mouse in his mouth.

00:06:38.591 --> 00:06:40.312
A mouse!

00:06:40.372 --> 00:06:42.083
Roxanne says.

00:06:42.143 --> 00:06:45.545
She screams again.

00:06:45.605 --> 00:06:51.186
In the morning Duncan and Leaking Larry are waiting.

00:06:51.246 --> 00:06:54.414
Roxanne and Obo are late.

00:06:54.474 --> 00:06:58.096
They get up at 11 o'clock.

00:06:58.155 --> 00:07:01.806
Good morning, Duncan says.

00:07:01.866 --> 00:07:04.798
Roxanne doesn't answer.

00:07:04.857 --> 00:07:10.370
She says to Larry, Larry, I don't like this place.

00:07:10.430 --> 00:07:12.540
I want to go home.

00:07:12.600 --> 00:07:18.023
But honey, Larry says, don't call me honey.

00:07:18.082 --> 00:07:19.880
Roxanne says.

00:07:19.940 --> 00:07:25.070
This castle is old, dark, and very cold.

00:07:25.130 --> 00:07:29.993
There's no electricity, no food, and no hot water.

00:07:30.053 --> 00:07:32.024
And I don't like it.

00:07:32.084 --> 00:07:33.885
Do you understand?

00:07:33.905 --> 00:07:40.859
Listen, honey, Larry says, we can build a big new house here.

00:07:40.919 --> 00:07:45.422
Our friends from California can come and stay.

00:07:45.482 --> 00:07:48.063
Duncan looks at Jock.

00:07:48.123 --> 00:07:50.930
Jock looks at Duncan.

00:07:50.990 --> 00:07:54.718
Build a big new house, they think.

00:07:54.778 --> 00:07:57.140
Oh no!

00:07:57.200 --> 00:08:02.454
Leaping Larry says, we want to see the island.

00:08:02.513 --> 00:08:08.508
Okay, Duncan says, we can go in my boat.

00:08:08.568 --> 00:08:13.622
Duncan, Larry and Roxanne getting to Duncan's boat.

00:08:13.682 --> 00:08:15.954
Jock gets in too.

00:08:16.013 --> 00:08:18.946
Bobo is with Roxanne.

00:08:19.006 --> 00:08:21.442
It's a beautiful day.

00:08:21.502 --> 00:08:25.028
But Roxanne isn't happy.

00:08:25.088 --> 00:08:28.220
What do you do all day?

00:08:28.280 --> 00:08:30.440
She asks Duncan.

00:08:30.500 --> 00:08:32.810
I go for walks.

00:08:32.870 --> 00:08:34.211
Duncan says.

00:08:34.271 --> 00:08:36.542
Sometimes I swim.

00:08:36.602 --> 00:08:40.022
And sometimes I catch fish.

00:08:40.082 --> 00:08:41.252
Oh.

00:08:41.312 --> 00:08:43.103
Roxanne says.

00:08:43.163 --> 00:08:46.164
That isn't very interesting.

00:08:46.224 --> 00:08:49.274
Listen, honey, Larry says.

00:08:49.334 --> 00:08:52.176
We can make the island interesting.

00:08:52.236 --> 00:08:55.128
I know people with film companies.

00:08:55.188 --> 00:08:57.880
They can come here and make films.

00:08:57.940 --> 00:09:00.322
Hundreds of films.

00:09:00.382 --> 00:09:02.853
Duncan looks at Jock.

00:09:02.912 --> 00:09:05.734
Jock looks at Duncan.

00:09:05.794 --> 00:09:08.966
Film companies, they think.

00:09:09.026 --> 00:09:11.348
Oh, no.

00:09:11.408 --> 00:09:15.181
Duncan is very unhappy.

00:09:15.241 --> 00:09:20.141
He doesn't want to sell his island and his castle to Larry.

00:09:20.201 --> 00:09:25.732
He doesn't want film companies or Larry's friends on the island.

00:09:25.792 --> 00:09:28.444
But what can Duncan do?

00:09:28.504 --> 00:09:32.736
The electricity company wants £5,000.

00:09:32.796 --> 00:09:35.208
He has no money.

00:09:35.268 --> 00:09:38.611
He can't stay in his castle.

00:09:38.671 --> 00:09:44.196
Duncan, Larry and Roxanne are all sitting in Duncan's boat.

00:09:44.256 --> 00:09:47.121
Jock and Bobo are wisdom.

00:09:47.181 --> 00:09:51.438
Suddenly, Jock sees a rabbit on the island.

00:09:51.498 --> 00:09:54.309
Jock loves catching rabbits.

00:09:54.369 --> 00:09:59.252
He jumps into the sea and starts to swim to the island.

00:09:59.312 --> 00:10:06.066
Bobo thinks, this is interesting, and he jumps in too.

00:10:06.126 --> 00:10:10.449
Bobo is in the water, Broxan screams.

00:10:10.509 --> 00:10:14.392
Jump into the sea lorry, get Bobo!

00:10:14.452 --> 00:10:17.138
But Larry doesn't move.

00:10:17.198 --> 00:10:19.794
Why are you ending?"

00:10:19.854 --> 00:10:21.326
Roxanne says.

00:10:21.386 --> 00:10:22.497
Jump in.

00:10:22.517 --> 00:10:26.079
But honey, Larry says.

00:10:26.140 --> 00:10:28.032
I can't swim.

00:10:28.092 --> 00:10:31.494
Can't swim, Roxanne says.

00:10:31.554 --> 00:10:34.346
She is very angry.

00:10:34.406 --> 00:10:37.228
Look, Duncan says.

00:10:37.288 --> 00:10:39.480
Bobo is okay.

00:10:39.540 --> 00:10:42.042
He's having a good time.

00:10:42.103 --> 00:10:45.968
Bobo is swimming in the water with jock.

00:10:46.028 --> 00:10:50.052
But Roxanne is very angry with Larry.

00:10:50.112 --> 00:10:53.696
You don't love me, she says.

00:10:53.756 --> 00:10:57.388
And you don't love me, Larry says.

00:10:57.448 --> 00:11:00.220
You only love, go go.

00:11:00.280 --> 00:11:03.643
You're right, Roxanne says.

00:11:03.703 --> 00:11:08.017
She stands in the boat and starts to hit Larry.

00:11:08.076 --> 00:11:11.358
Don't do that, Duncan says.

00:11:11.418 --> 00:11:13.248
The boat moves.

00:11:13.308 --> 00:11:16.798
Roxanne falls into the water.

00:11:16.858 --> 00:11:19.400
She starts to scream.

00:11:19.459 --> 00:11:23.212
Roxanne is making a lot of noise.

00:11:23.272 --> 00:11:27.384
Jock sees Roxanne in the water with Bobo.

00:11:27.444 --> 00:11:29.274
What are they doing?

00:11:29.334 --> 00:11:31.836
Are they playing a new game?

00:11:31.896 --> 00:11:34.497
Jock wants to play too.

00:11:34.557 --> 00:11:37.048
He swings to Bobo.

00:11:37.108 --> 00:11:38.929
Don't want any!

00:11:38.989 --> 00:11:41.225
Roxanne screams.

00:11:41.285 --> 00:11:45.051
Duncan brings the boat near Roxanne.

00:11:45.111 --> 00:11:48.022
Roxanne gets into the boat.

00:11:48.082 --> 00:11:51.693
Then Bobo gets into the boat.

00:11:51.753 --> 00:11:55.824
Roxanne is very angry.

00:11:55.884 --> 00:11:59.395
Take me back to California.

00:11:59.455 --> 00:12:03.816
Now, she says to Larry.

00:12:03.876 --> 00:12:11.229
Later, Larry, Roxanne and Bobo get into their helicopter.

00:12:11.289 --> 00:12:12.930
Goodbye!"

00:12:12.990 --> 00:12:14.682
Duncan says.

00:12:14.742 --> 00:12:18.373
Larry and Roxanne don't answer.

00:12:18.433 --> 00:12:21.554
The helicopter goes away.

00:12:21.614 --> 00:12:24.256
Duncan smiles at Jock.

00:12:24.316 --> 00:12:26.748
He's very happy.

00:12:26.808 --> 00:12:32.790
Leaping laddy isn't going to buy our island, he says.

00:12:32.850 --> 00:12:35.091
That's good.

00:12:35.151 --> 00:12:39.744
But Duncan has big money problems.

00:12:39.804 --> 00:12:43.938
Leaping Larry doesn't want to buy the island.

00:12:43.998 --> 00:12:50.323
But where can Duncan get £5,000 for the electricity company?

00:12:50.383 --> 00:12:56.158
Later, Duncan telephones Mr Moneybags in London.

00:12:56.218 --> 00:13:01.852
Leaping Larry telephoned me, Mr Moneybag says.

00:13:01.912 --> 00:13:04.614
He doesn't like your island.

00:13:04.674 --> 00:13:07.171
He doesn't want to buy it.

00:13:07.230 --> 00:13:10.977
And I'm not going to sell it for you now.

00:13:11.037 --> 00:13:13.288
It's your problem.

00:13:13.348 --> 00:13:15.918
Goodbye.

00:13:15.978 --> 00:13:20.830
Duncan goes for a long walk with Jock.

00:13:20.890 --> 00:13:23.301
He's very unhappy.

00:13:23.361 --> 00:13:26.862
They walk to a place across the island.

00:13:26.922 --> 00:13:30.514
And there Duncan sees a girl.

00:13:30.574 --> 00:13:35.202
She's looking at the sea and she's painting a picture.

00:13:35.262 --> 00:13:38.980
Near her is a small boat.

00:13:39.040 --> 00:13:43.482
Good afternoon, Duncan says.

00:13:43.542 --> 00:13:46.392
The girl looks at Duncan.

00:13:46.452 --> 00:13:48.243
She's beautiful.

00:13:48.303 --> 00:13:50.434
He likes her.

00:13:50.494 --> 00:13:52.244
Who are you?

00:13:52.304 --> 00:13:53.624
She asks.

00:13:53.684 --> 00:13:56.866
What do you want?

00:13:56.926 --> 00:14:01.157
I'm Duncan McTavish, Duncan says.

00:14:01.217 --> 00:14:02.747
I live here.

00:14:02.807 --> 00:14:05.255
Lana is my island.

00:14:05.315 --> 00:14:08.834
And this is my dog, Jock.

00:14:08.894 --> 00:14:11.276
Jock looks at the girl.

00:14:11.336 --> 00:14:13.616
He likes her too.

00:14:13.676 --> 00:14:17.829
Blanna is your island, the girl says.

00:14:17.889 --> 00:14:21.261
Oh, I'm Jean Stewart.

00:14:21.321 --> 00:14:22.872
I'm a teacher.

00:14:22.932 --> 00:14:26.274
I work in a school across the sea.

00:14:26.334 --> 00:14:30.666
Today is a holiday and the school is closed.

00:14:30.726 --> 00:14:33.626
I came here in my boat.

00:14:33.686 --> 00:14:36.614
I wanted to paint your island.

00:14:36.674 --> 00:14:42.195
The light is very good and the colours are very beautiful.

00:14:42.255 --> 00:14:45.546
I can paint good pictures here."

00:14:45.606 --> 00:14:48.827
Duncan looks at Jean's picture.

00:14:48.887 --> 00:14:51.158
Yes, he says.

00:14:51.218 --> 00:14:54.008
Your picture is very good.

00:14:54.068 --> 00:14:57.079
Thank you, Jean says.

00:14:57.139 --> 00:15:01.377
Duncan and Jean talk for a long time.

00:15:01.438 --> 00:15:04.806
Where do you live, Jean asks?

00:15:04.866 --> 00:15:08.587
I live in a castle, Duncan says.

00:15:08.647 --> 00:15:10.818
Come and see it.

00:15:10.878 --> 00:15:15.070
Duncan, Jean and Jock go to the castle.

00:15:15.130 --> 00:15:19.721
Your castle is beautiful, Jean says.

00:15:19.781 --> 00:15:22.122
Yes, Duncan says.

00:15:22.182 --> 00:15:25.262
But it's very cold and dark.

00:15:25.322 --> 00:15:27.684
There's no electricity.

00:15:27.744 --> 00:15:30.001
I have no money.

00:15:30.061 --> 00:15:36.300
I love my island very much, but I can't make money from it."

00:15:36.360 --> 00:15:39.072
Jean looks at the castle.

00:15:39.132 --> 00:15:44.104
Suddenly she says, yes, you can.

00:15:44.164 --> 00:15:45.425
How?

00:15:45.485 --> 00:15:47.076
Duncan asks.

00:15:47.136 --> 00:15:51.928
People can come here for holidays, Jean says.

00:15:51.988 --> 00:15:55.530
They can paint pictures of your island.

00:15:55.590 --> 00:16:00.808
I can teach them, and they can stay in your castle.

00:16:00.868 --> 00:16:04.026
We can make a lot of money.

00:16:04.086 --> 00:16:07.037
Duncan looks at Jog.

00:16:07.097 --> 00:16:10.088
Jog looks at Duncan.

00:16:10.148 --> 00:16:14.159
You're right, Duncan says.

00:16:14.219 --> 00:16:20.451
Now, MacTavish painting the holidays are very famous.

00:16:20.511 --> 00:16:24.742
Every year, many visitors come to the island.

00:16:24.802 --> 00:16:27.083
They stay in the castle.

00:16:27.143 --> 00:16:31.152
They go for walks and paint beautiful pictures.

00:16:31.212 --> 00:16:34.911
They take their pictures back to their homes.

00:16:34.972 --> 00:16:40.024
The rooms in the castle aren't cold and dark now.

00:16:40.084 --> 00:16:43.796
Duncan and Jean have a lot of money.

00:16:43.856 --> 00:16:47.908
There is no problem with the electricity company.

00:16:47.969 --> 00:16:51.842
And Jean makes very good food.

00:16:51.902 --> 00:16:55.864
The visitors are very happy.

00:16:55.924 --> 00:17:00.040
Duncan and Jean are married now.

00:17:00.100 --> 00:17:04.756
They have two children, a boy and a girl.

00:17:04.817 --> 00:17:08.769
Jock loves playing with the children.

00:17:08.829 --> 00:17:13.192
Duncan often sits in his little boat.

00:17:13.252 --> 00:17:19.756
Sometimes he catches a fish, but usually he sleeps.

00:17:19.817 --> 00:17:22.728
He's a happy man.

